  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed change of use of the existing outbuilding to provide a self-contained residential unit would cause harm to the character of the application site and wider neighbourhood and would be contrary to adopted Local Plan Policies SC1 (Housing Growth) CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations) and the intent of the Residential Extension Guidelines SPD. ",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development would cause harm to the living conditions of the existing and future occupiers of the application site and its adjoining neighbours by reason of loss of privacy, overlooking, increased activities, noise and disturbance, and would be contrary to Local Policies CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations).",
    "Reason : 3 - The converted outbuilding would fail to meet the minimum floor requirement for a self-contained house of its size. The scheme has failed to demonstrate that, subsequent to the development, adequate amenity space would be afforded to both the dwellings at this application site. It would fail to fail to comply with London Plan policy D6 (Housing quality and standards) and Local Plan policy SC5 (Housing quality and standards).  ",
    "Reason : 4 - The scheme has failed to demonstrate that adequate transport and servicing provisions, and safe access would be afforded within the development. It would be contrary to Local Policies EC2(Developing a sustainable local transport network) and EQ8 (Sustainable waste management) and London Policy D12 (Fire Safety). "
  ],
